<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's money base up to 2.56 bln sucres in Sept.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's money base up to 2.56 bln sucres in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's money base rose 0.87 percent to 2.56 billion sucres in September, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In August, the money base grew 4.1 percent to 2.53 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The bank did not give any reason for the increase.</p>
<p>In the first nine months of 1996, the money base increased 6.17 percent.</p>
<p>The money base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres, up from 1.85 billion sucres at the end of 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
